+++
title: Finishing is a different skill than starting
coach: sam
date: 2025-05-02
domains: creativity
+++

Starting a project and finishing one draw on almost none of the same
muscles. Starting rewards momentum and a good idea. Finishing rewards
tolerance for a draft that's worse than the one in your head.

Most of the writers I work with are good at starting. That's not what
brought them to coaching. What brought them in is a drawer of projects
that all stopped at roughly the same point — not from lack of talent,
but from never having practiced the specific, unglamorous work of
staying with something past the point it stopped feeling exciting.
